      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. I'll improve understandability by:\n1. Removing unused imports and unused class fields (`MAX_LENGTH`, `TEST`, `PARIS`)\n2. Making the leap year loop self-documenting using `YearMonth.lengthOfMonth()` and named constants instead of magic numbers\n3. Renaming loop variable from `i` to `day` for clarity\n4. Adding an assertion message to pinpoint failuresThe improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes unused imports and class fields, replaces magic numbers with `YearMonth.lengthOfMonth()` for self-documenting month lengths, renames the loop variable from `i` to `day`, and adds descriptive assertion messages — all while preserving the original runtime behaviour exactly."
